B.Jt=new A.bk(34,"pass\xe9 compos\xe9 with avoir","A2","Use pass\xe9 compos\xe9 for completed past actions. Most verbs use avoir.","present of `avoir` + past participle",B.X3,"-er \u2192 -\xe9, -ir \u2192 -i, -re \u2192 -u; many irregular: faire \u2192 fait, prendre \u2192 pris.","Build it in two parts: conjugate `avoir` in the present, then add the past participle.","Use this tense for a finished past action: one thing happened and is complete. The auxiliary changes with the subject; the past participle usually stays fixed with `avoir` at A2.",B.Ty,B.Un,"Do not conjugate the second verb: write `j'ai parl\xe9`, not `j'ai parle` or `je suis parl\xe9`.")
