B.Jy=new A.bk(37,"Pronoun y","A2","y replaces a place or \xe0 + thing phrase.","`y` before conjugated verb; before infinitive with two verbs",B.Nc,"y cannot replace people. Use stressed pronouns: Je pense \xe0 elle.","Use `y` to avoid repeating a place or an `\xe0 + thing` phrase.","`Y` usually means `there` or `to it`. It goes before the conjugated verb, but if there is an infinitive, it often goes before the infinitive.",B.Qo,B.a1d,"Do not use `y` for people. Say `Je pense \xe0 elle`, not `j'y pense`, when `elle` is a person.")
