B.Jz=new A.bk(39,"Pronoun en","A2","en replaces de + noun, quantities, and partitive expressions.","`en` before conjugated verb; before infinitive in two-verb structures",B.Mv,"Keep the quantity word after verb: J'en veux deux.","Use `en` for `de + noun`, quantities, and partitive ideas like `du pain`.","`En` often means `some`, `of it`, or `of them`. It replaces the noun phrase, but numbers and quantity words usually remain after the verb.",B.Xv,B.N5,"Keep the number or amount: `J'en ai deux`, not `J'en ai` if the important information is `two`.")
